Reason: keep a unit's Life and max Life in 64 bits in the core, so a monster of any size is the number it is (native 64-bit health Part 1, Patch A; plan docs/proposals/core-64bit-health.md section 2.3, changed by the client-half brief of 2026-10-16). The update-field layout grows by two dwords, UNIT_FIELD_HEALTH_HI and UNIT_FIELD_MAXHEALTH_HI, and Unit::WriteHealthFields is the only writer of the four dwords: the real Life, with no projection. Only a rebuilt client reads this layout. Every place the narrowing census (a build whose Life getters refuse each conversion to a type under 64 bits) found a Life cut to 32 bits is fixed by its class; the list is core-patches/tests/life64_census.tsv.

